{"name":"Rainbow","hex":"#f6bfbc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rainbow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Rainbow Guides, a Girl Guide movement for younger girls."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in San Diego County, California, United States.","A town in the Shire of Hindmarsh and the Shire of Yarriambiack, western Victoria, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rainbow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rainbow","blocks":[{"text":"A rainbow is an optical phenomenon caused by refraction, internal reflection and dispersion of light in water droplets resulting in a continuous spectrum of light appearing in the sky. The rainbow takes the form of a multicoloured circular arc. Rainbows caused by sunlight always appear in the section of sky directly opposite the sun. Rainbows can be caused by many forms of airborne water. These include not only rain, but also mist, spray, and airborne dew."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg/330px-Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow"},{"title":"Rainbow (Mariah Carey album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rainbow is the seventh studio album by American singer-songwriter Mariah Carey. It was released on November 2, 1999, by Columbia Records. The album followed Butterfly (1997), in which she adopted a new image and fully transitioned into the urban contemporary market. Rainbow contains hip-hop–influenced R&B tracks and a variety of ballads. Carey produced the album mainly with Jimmy Jam & Terry Lewis, who replaced Walter Afanasieff, the main balladeer Carey worked with throughout the 1990s. As a result of her divorce from Sony Music CEO Tommy Mottola, Carey had more control over the musical style of Rainbow; she collaborated with several hip-hop artists such as Jay-Z, Snoop Dogg, Master P and Mystikal as well as female rappers Da Brat and Missy Elliott. Other collaborations include Joe, Usher and boy band 98 Degrees."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Mariah_Carey_Rainbow.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_(Mariah_Carey_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rainbow in Moshav Aviel, Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/500px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/1280px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/500px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A colourful rainbow and ring-billed gull","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARing-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_(52910).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Raindrop_optics.jpg/500px-Raindrop_optics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"